From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 22:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: describe the qcom,pshold restart
 register

msm8998 is the only SoC in its family with no restart node: msm8916, msm8994,
msm8953, sdm630 and sc8280xp all describe qcom,pshold. The downstream
msm8998.dtsi has it at the same address this adds, 0x10ac000, so the
description is simply missing upstream.

Describe it. Note that on its own this changes nothing: msm-poweroff registers
its restart handler at priority 128 and the PSCI handler sits at 129, so PSCI
still performs every restart.

That is deliberate, and the reason is worth recording. Raising msm-poweroff
above PSCI was tried and reverted, because mainline's reset is only half of
what this SoC needs. Downstream does:

	msm_restart_prepare(cmd);      /* latch the PMIC warm or hard */
	halt_spmi_pmic_arbiter();      /* SCM_IO_DISABLE_PMIC_ARBITER */
	deassert_ps_hold();
	mdelay(10000);

and deassert_ps_hold() issues SCM_IO_DEASSERT_PS_HOLD, falling through to
__raw_writel(0, msm_ps_hold) only "in case the scm_call returns". Mainline
implements only that fallback, and on msm8998 the bare write is ignored: with
msm-poweroff winning the arbitration, an orderly reboot stopped resetting the
SoC and the hardware watchdog rescued it ~30 s later, measured as a 49 s
down-gap and androidboot.bootreason=watchdog where it had previously read
reboot. Mainline qcom_scm has no SCM_SVC_PWR support at all, so making this
work needs a new SCM call, not a DT change.

Keep the node so the hardware is described correctly and so that work has
somewhere to attach.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -4303,6 +4303,11 @@
 			power-domains = <&mmcc BIMC_SMMU_GDSC>;
 		};
 
+		restart@10ac000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,pshold";
+			reg = <0x010ac000 0x4>;
+		};
+
 		imem@146bf000 {
 			compatible = "simple-mfd";
 			reg = <0x146bf000 0x1000>;
-- 
